cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, cite the paper and this release."
title: "esp32s3-inference: Memory-aware transformer inference and embedded model runtime for ESP32-S3"
abstract: >-
  Firmware, raw measurement logs and analysis scripts for a 260K-parameter
  decoder-only transformer running at batch size one on an ESP32-S3, with the
  key/value cache stored as int8 in external PSRAM and attention mapped onto
  the 128-bit integer SIMD unit. At 512-token context the final build sustains
  166.6 decode forwards/s, equivalent to 168.25 sampled tokens/s. That is
  2.898x the sampled-token rate of the same-tree fp32 single-core baseline
  (58.06 sampled tokens/s). The 512-sample harness performs 507 decode
  forwards. Firmware, tools and build configuration are GPL-3.0-only. The
  bundled model and tokenizer retain their upstream MIT licence. Documentation
  and figures are CC BY 4.0. The submitted manuscript and production files are
  not included in this repository.
